    "rock_scatter": {
      "_comment": "SHARED PHYSICAL FACT (CLAUDE.md non-negotiable 19). Read by BOTH the Pass 2 landscape material's scree sub-surface mask AND Pass 3's talus mesh scatter. Defined once here; neither consumer may keep its own copy. These are properties of rock, not style knobs.",
      "repose_deg": 35.0,
      "cliff_source_slope_deg": 45.0,
      "source_smooth_m": 16.0,
      "runout_m": 120.0,
      "mfd_exponent": 1.3,
      "max_steps": 2400,
      "saturation": 0.03,
      "_max_steps_note": "RESOLUTION-DEPENDENT, and the ONLY member of this block that is not a property of rock. It is a solver ITERATION BUDGET denominated in CELLS. talus_deposit decays carried mass by trans=exp(-spacing_m/L) per step, so at 1 m spacing mass decays 0.83%/step where 4 m spacing decays 3.3%, and the starting supply is 16x larger on 16x the cells. 600 (tuned at 2017) refused to converge at 8129 with 108.2550 units still in transit; ~1450 are needed and 2400 = 600 x (8129/2017) gives margin. SCALE THIS WITH 1/spacing."
    },
    "canopy": {
      "_comment": "SHARED PHYSICAL FACT (CLAUDE.md non-negotiable 19), sibling to rock_scatter. The canopy radius is a MEASURED property of the tree, not a style knob, and any consumer that clusters under trees reads it from here. Currently read by rock_scatter.py via placement_priors.canopy_occupancy for Pass 5 ground clutter.",
      "_source": "Free/_measured/fir_tree_01.json -> object fir_tree_01_c_LOD0, dims_xyz [6.305939, 5.96624, 14.520583] m. radius_m is the mean horizontal half-extent: (6.305939 + 5.96624) / 4 = 3.068 m. This is the mesh PLACED as Conifer (foliage.species[].mesh ends fir_tree_01_c_LOD0), not the higher-poly _a or _b variants, which measure 6.534 x 6.427 and 5.613 x 6.057.",
      "plan": "alpine_Conifer.json",
      "radius_m": 3.068
    }
